cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FungiForge, please cite it as below."
title: "FungiForge: reproducible fungal genomics from Oxford Nanopore, Illumina, or hybrid reads (assembly -> annotation -> antifungal resistance -> biosynthetic gene clusters -> comparative analysis)"
abstract: >-
  FungiForge is an organism-agnostic Nextflow DSL2 + Python pipeline for fungal
  genomics from Oxford Nanopore, Illumina, or a hybrid of both. Each isolate is routed
  automatically by its reads: long-read assembly (Flye + Medaka, optionally Illumina-polished)
  when ONT data are present, or short-read assembly (SPAdes) from Illumina alone. It then
  performs eukaryotic genome annotation, ITS and whole-genome identification, antifungal-
  resistance calling, mobile-element/transposon/mycovirus detection, biosynthetic gene
  cluster discovery, novelty assessment and One Health comparative analysis. It is the
  fungal sibling of the forge family (CaptureForge, CallForge, MethylForge).
